WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.975
The answer to check three: one
notice, with the latest window.

2
00:00:03.975 --> 00:00:06.100
Scene four, AWS.

3
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.922
AWS's documentation says AWS
Health tells each account

4
00:00:09.922 --> 00:00:13.162
which of its instances
will be retired, and when.

5
00:00:13.162 --> 00:00:15.710
AWS has its own actionability field,

6
00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:19.787
and when it says action required,
that's the provider's word.

7
00:00:19.787 --> 00:00:24.734
But a scheduled change that names a retirement
or lifecycle event without that flag

8
00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:27.419
could look optional, so
the kit makes it action

9
00:00:27.419 --> 00:00:29.751
required by its own
rule, due at its start.

10
00:00:29.751 --> 00:00:33.906
Two things to know: the Health API
needs a qualifying support plan,

11
00:00:33.906 --> 00:00:37.062
and the GovCloud partition
has a single endpoint.

12
00:00:37.062 --> 00:00:40.420
The kit names the partition,
and checks the caller is in it.
